why Starts now at 20 with a shield; a hauberk at 28, then a coif, leggings and gauntlets from three smiths.

# The Alliance Warrior armor chain: Yorus Barleybrew, The Rethban Gauntlet and
# The Shieldsmith (1698, 1699, 1702, level 20-22: Furen's Favor), Fire Hardened
# Mail and Furen's Armor (1701, 1782, level 28: Fire Hardened Hauberk), then
# three smiths: Grimand Elmore in Stormwind (Burning Blood 1705, Grimand's
# Armor 1706: Fire Hardened Coif), Mathiel in Darnassus (Sunscorched Shells
# 1710, Mathiel's Armor 1711: Fire Hardened Leggings) and Klockmort
# Spannerspan in Ironforge (Iron Coral 1708, Klockmort's Creation 1709: Fire
# Hardened Gauntlets).
# Furen sends each race to one smith with a breadcrumb (Grimand Elmore 1700
# Human, Mathiel 1703 Night Elf, Klockmort Spannerspan 1704 Dwarf and Gnome),
# but the smiths' own quests have no prerequisite and no race limit (TDB:
# 1705, 1708 and 1710 PrevQuestID 0, any Alliance race; quest-notes: any
# warrior can talk to Mathiel directly), so any Alliance warrior can earn all
# three pieces; Skyborne get no breadcrumb and are sent to Grimand here.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the chain,
# objectives and places (the Rethban Caverns point is the quest's own
# objective position); the knowledge base's drop table (Scorched Spider Fang
# 100%, Charred Horn and Galvanized Horn 80%, Burning Blood and Burning Rock
# 80%, the shells and coral 100% per object); quest-notes for the gauntlet's
# 1-hour timer and drink, the gnolls, the few chimaeras, Roogug and the way
# through Razorfen Kraul, Gutspill's patrol, the 9 shells and 10 corals and
# their respawns, the murlocs' nets; Forever's Warrior class quest list
# (data/local/quest-audit/) for the rewards and Forever's changes (none for
# this chain); the Razorfen Kraul entrance from data/forever/dungeons.json
# (The Barrens 42.9,90.2, live frame). Roogug, who drops the Vial of
# Phlogiston, has no spawn in the data: he is a quilboar elite inside
# Razorfen Kraul (zone 491; a Classic quest wiki's page on the Vial of
# Phlogiston).
# No leveling guide takes this chain: it needs a dungeon (Razorfen Kraul) and
# runs from Redridge to Stonetalon, the Wetlands and the capitals.
# Fire Hardened Mail and the pieces after it (level 28-30) are near or above
# the beta's level cap: that part is written from the data, not from play.

step Yorus Barleybrew (Stormwind)
  only Human,Skyborne
  zone Stormwind City
  tip At 20, Wu Shen, beside Ilsa Corbin in the warrior trainers' building of Old Town, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
  level 20
  accept 1698 npc 5479                        -- Wu Shen

step Yorus Barleybrew (Ironforge)
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  tip At 20, Kelv Sternhammer, the warrior trainer of Ironforge, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
  level 20
  accept 1698 npc 5113                        -- Kelv Sternhammer

step Yorus Barleybrew (Darnassus)
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip At 20, Darnath Bladesinger, the warrior trainer of Darnassus, sends you to Yorus Barleybrew in Redridge.
  level 20
  accept 1698 npc 7315                        -- Darnath Bladesinger

step Yorus Barleybrew
  zone Redridge Mountains
  tip Yorus Barleybrew sits in the inn at Lakeshire. His test is timed: before you take it, clear the Redridge gnolls on the path to the Rethban Caverns in the hills north-west of Lakeshire, including the two on the rock by the cave mouth (climb it from its right side).
  turnin 1698                                 -- Yorus Barleybrew
  accept 1699

step The Rethban Gauntlet
  tip You have one hour, and Yorus's Barleybrew Scalder leaves you drunk for 8-10 minutes. Run north-west into the Rethban Caverns, keeping close to the cliff wall to miss most gnoll packs, and go in as far as the first fork; then come back to Yorus (from the ridge you can jump down into Lakeshire). Dying and releasing your spirit fails the quest: abandon it and Yorus gives it again.
  complete 1699                               -- Enter the Rethban Caverns and come back
  turnin 1699
  accept 1702

step The Shieldsmith
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Furen Longbeard works in the Dwarven District of Stormwind. He takes the Cask of Scalder (lost it? abandon the quest and Yorus gives a new one) and gives you Furen's Favor, a shield; Fire Hardened Mail is a level 28 quest, with Furen's Instructions listing what it needs.
  turnin 1702 reward 6970                     -- Furen Longbeard
  accept 1701

step Scorched Spider Fangs
  zone Wetlands
  tip You need 50 fangs. The Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers (level 21-22) crawl in the middle of the Wetlands, north of Dun Algaz; every one drops a fang. They poison; back in 5 minutes.
  collect 6838 x50 quest 1701.1               -- Scorched Spider Fang

step Charred and Galvanized Horns
  zone Stonetalon Mountains
  tip The chimaeras live south-west of Sun Rock Retreat in the Charred Vale: you need 12 Charred Horns from the Fledgling (level 25-27) and Young Chimaeras (23-25), four kills in five, and the Galvanized Horn from the Chimaera Matriarch (28, the big one), also four in five. Only three Fledglings, two Young and one Matriarch live there, each back in 5 minutes, so expect to wait. Fledglings and the Matriarch spit Corrosive Poison, the Young cast Lightning Bolt. Alliance: fly to Stonetalon Peak and head south.
  collect 6839 x12 quest 1701.2               -- Charred Horn, from the young chimaeras
  collect 6840 quest 1701.3                   -- Galvanized Horn, from the Chimaera Matriarch

step Roogug in Razorfen Kraul
  zone The Barrens
  tip Roogug is an elite quilboar (level 28) inside Razorfen Kraul, the dungeon at the south end of the Barrens; a five-player dungeon: needs a group of five, and his guards come with him. Inside take the left path at the first fork, cross the root bridge, go past the big empty cauldron: he is in a dead end on the right, with about ten elites on the way. He casts Lightning Bolt and calls Earth Rumblers. The vial always drops.
  collect 6841 quest 1701.4 @42.9,90.2 live group 5 -- Vial of Phlogiston, from Roogug

step Furen's Armor
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Back to Furen Longbeard in the Dwarven District for the hauberk. He then sends you to the smith of your race; the other two smiths' pieces are open to you as well: talk to them directly.
  turnin 1701                                 -- Furen Longbeard
  accept 1782
  turnin 1782 reward 6972
  accept 1700 only Human
  accept 1703 only NightElf
  accept 1704 only Dwarf,Gnome

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Grimand Elmore (Human, Skyborne): the coif

step Grimand Elmore
  only Human,Skyborne
  tip Grimand Elmore keeps the weapon shop in the north-west of the Dwarven District, a short walk from Furen. He wants 20 Burning Blood and the Burning Rock.
  turnin 1700 only Human                      -- Grimand Elmore
  accept 1705

step Burning Blood
  only Human,Skyborne
  zone Duskwood
  tip The Nightbane worgen of Duskwood (Dark Runners, Vile Fangs, Shadow Weavers, Worgen and Tainted Ones, level 26-31) south and west of Darkshire drop the Burning Blood four kills in five. Gutspill (level 32, not elite) carries the Burning Rock (also four in five): he walks between the inside and the mouth of the Roland's Doom mine south-east of Darkshire, so wait at the entrance and pull him outside. Gutspill and the Tainted Ones poison and howl; Vile Fangs cause Infected Wound.
  collect 6844 x20 quest 1705.1               -- Burning Blood, from the Nightbane worgen
  collect 6845 quest 1705.2                   -- Burning Rock, from Gutspill

step Grimand's Armor
  only Human,Skyborne
  zone Stormwind City
  turnin 1705                                 -- Grimand Elmore
  accept 1706
  turnin 1706 reward 6971

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mathiel (Night Elf): the leggings

step Mathiel
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Mathiel works on the south side of the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. He wants 20 Sunscorched Shells.
  turnin 1703                                 -- Mathiel
  accept 1710

step Sunscorched Shells
  only NightElf
  zone Thousand Needles
  tip The shells lie on the ground under the wyvern nests at Highperch in western Thousand Needles, deeper into the gorge. Only nine exist and each returns 3 minutes after you pick it, so you will wait; some shell-like things there cannot be looted. Highperch Wyverns (level 28-31) guard them and sometimes come several at once.
  collect 6849 x20 quest 1710.1               -- Sunscorched Shell

step Mathiel's Armor
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  turnin 1710                                 -- Mathiel
  accept 1711
  turnin 1711 reward 6973

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Klockmort Spannerspan (Dwarf, Gnome): the gauntlets

step Klockmort Spannerspan
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  tip Ride the Deeprun Tram from Stormwind to Ironforge. Klockmort Spannerspan, a gnome smith, works in Tinker Town near the engineering trainers. He wants 20 Searing Coral.
  turnin 1704                                 -- Klockmort Spannerspan
  accept 1708

step Iron Coral
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Wetlands
  tip The Iron Coral grows on the sea floor just south of Menethil Harbor, by the murloc huts and a wrecked boat: eight there and two south-east of the harbor, each back in 3 minutes, so you will wait for respawns to reach 20. The murlocs can net you underwater: watch your breath, and a Draught of Water Breathing removes the risk.
  collect 6848 x20 quest 1708.1               -- Searing Coral, from Iron Coral

step Klockmort's Creation
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  turnin 1708                                 -- Klockmort Spannerspan
  accept 1709
  turnin 1709 reward 6974
